      "message": "the improvement in quality is great and consistent with the direction i\u0027m heading, so i do want to land this, but I expect it to break \u0027golden tests\u0027.  applications that use libyuv write tests that expect exactly the same results as in the past.\nOne work around is add a compile time macro that is off by default and make users set the macro to true to get the improved quality.\nBut I prefer try to land it without that hackery.  LGTM\n\nI did some rotate changes this week and one idea is 2 step row functions to handle complex types like rgb24.  It would take take 3 vectors worth of rgb per row, split it into 3 tiles (splitrgb), use existing transposeplane, then merge.  does per 16x16 tile it would be reasonable efficient.  on arm a custom row function can do native rgb with the same approach of ld3 into 3 tiles of 16x16, use 3 transposes, then st3.  A similar idea could be applied to scaling.\nprovide a row function api, implement it as a c 2 pass wrapper.  The row_common.cc has examples of \u0027avx2\u0027 row functions that do this for rgb24, while allowing neon to do them natively, since its easy on arm and riscv - use ld3.",
